* ------------------------------------------------------------------
* Example Pin Definition File for QSymGen
* ------------------------------------------------------------------
*
* TODO:  Revise this after working through code
*
* Pin Definitions:  DIR NAME ALTTEXT [* COMMENT]
*
* Where: DIR = Pin direction: I (input), O (output), B (bi-directional, i.e, GPIO), or X (unused for spacing).
*        NAME = Pin name.  (Duplicates are allowed.)
*        ALTTEXT = Additional text to include on symbol, e.g., alternate pin functions.
*        COMMENT = Optional comment.  (Space required before '*'.)
*
* ---------------------------------
*
* Notes:
*   Leading spaces are removed when parsing.
*   Lines beginning with '*' are comments and are ignored.
*   Blank lines are ignored.
*
* ---------------------------------
*
* Example:
*

*
* M = Manufacturer [optional, will appear as text info in symbol/schematic]
*
M Microchip 

*
* P = Part #(s) [optional, will appear as text info in symbol/schematic]
* TODO:  Default to stem file name (done).  Make alt part numbers separate item?  Add to symbol description?
*
P PIC16F1521x PIC16F15213/PIC16F15214 * Alt parts

*
* D = descriptive text for symbol and DLL block [optional]
*
D Microchip PIC16F15213/PIC16F15214

*
* Pin Definitions
*
I VDD
B RA0 ICSPDAT 
B RA1 ICSPCLK
I RA2 MCLR/VPP
B RA3 
B RA4 
B RA5 
I VSS

*
*** EOF ***